# S-INFO-1: Defense-in-depth guard — prevent raw brain DB blobs from being committed.
# Option A (frozen-brain-snapshot) was explicitly rejected in the agentic-x183 Design
# precisely to avoid committing raw SQLite blobs. This .gitignore ensures that a
# careless --out *.sqlite or a copied brain can never be accidentally staged here.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal

# agentic-7r28: the default `cerebro eval --out` target is a local scratch
# baseline so a bare `cerebro eval` never clobbers the committed reference
# (docs/evals/baseline.json). Updating the committed baseline is deliberate:
# `cerebro eval -p <brain> --out docs/evals/baseline.json`.
baseline.local.json
